  "next_engineering": {
    "status": "DESIGN_CONSTRAINTS_ONLY_NOT_IMPLEMENTED",
    "steps": [
      "Build a private same-invocation Trainer read-set returning actual observed E/D/T signatures and Candidate bytes/current proof from the one original occupied SourceBound lane; freeze exact context, identity, nonce and physical tail. Root cannot create it from stored DTOs.",
      "Have an Evaluation read transaction consume a same-invocation full predecessor vector and compare its original before/after set. The new374 B proof must be audited before any competing implementation.",
      "Deduplicate B's shared original Trainer only inside one actual B read window, retaining every member's actual journals, Source/witness, exact signatures and the final physical tail. Do not treat distinct member connections as aliases.",
      "Carry an actual full same-call vector upward through S/C/Root so the checkpoint does not recursively reconstruct an already authenticated prefix. No result survives the invocation as CURRENT or authorizes Fresh.",
      "Recompute every retained endpoint counter including Version/issuer/factory/readiness and actual setup; publish no fits128 claim from the localT2 or B-only improvement.",
      "Require real withdrawal-between-before/after, changed full signature, distinct source identity, cancellation, dropped/recovered channel and no-second-effect regressions without raising caps/deadlines."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
      "Holding a Trainer lane while a B callback recursively asks the same Trainer can deadlock or hit Busy; avoid recursive owner-lock cycles.",
      "A cached model artifact is not a cached current proof.",
      "Root RunStart and external original custody remain separate from starting a runtime."
    ]
  },
